WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:01.580
Why
is ‘The furniture

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.792
are expensive’
wrong?

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:05.861
Furniture
contains many

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:08.003
things: a chair,
a table,

00:00:08.043 --> 00:00:09.731
a sofa, a bed.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:11.481
But English
groups them

00:00:11.521 --> 00:00:13.027
together,
and names them

00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:14.672
as one unit.

00:00:15.103 --> 00:00:16.447
Unit means one.

00:00:16.487 --> 00:00:18.242
And one is always
singular.

00:00:18.282 --> 00:00:20.085
We can’t add
s to one.

00:00:20.537 --> 00:00:21.928
So:

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:23.407
‘The furniture
is expensive.’

